Z||000003||grgoyl86||10-07-2001||11:48 AM||||I have an exhaust made by IRM, and intended for the V6. It "splices" into the old system near the RR axle, comes out pas the trunk and splits in two, making a quad exhaust!  8^)<BR>There is no muffler in this system, but it uses Holley Resonator Tips (4 of them, of course).<BR>Oh, and it's all stainless steel.<BR>It is loud, but not obnoxious. Not that loud buzzing sound like all those Hondas and stuff with 36" dia tailpipes.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Why do we park in driveways and drive on parkways?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||10-07-2001||12:04 PM||||The GT I just bought has no muffler and uses resonator tips. It is louder than I would like.<BR>What could I do to mellow it out?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero5||10-07-2001||05:13 PM||||Marians (LVMY88) has what is the loudest (when stepped on), 4 cyl. exhaust I have heard to date. It is a custom exhaust that eliminates the muffler, and splits the pipes after the cat to stock GT tips.<P>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000006||BlackDragon||10-07-2001||07:32 PM||||im making one for my duke. i will take pics of it when im done. basicaly what im doing is taking out the cat, and running it out the back of the passenger side.<P>------------------<BR>We are all different for a reason.....<BR>you can read a persons soul through there eyes.....<BR>he who argues with a fool is probably one himself.....<BR>big cars may be fast, but i can corner.....<P>BlackDragonsEmail@yahoo.com||||reg||1
